 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** VIPER is $O(1)$ per sample and is noted as computationally faster than Levy's method [S2, unofficial]. Depth Measure is $O(1)$ per sample [S3, unofficial]. UBS involves matrix operations (Cholesky solve, inversion) which are generally more expensive, scaling with the dimensionality of the covariance matrix [S4, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** VIPER is noted as computationally faster than Levy's method [S2, unofficial]. Depth Measure complexity is Not given in the sources. UBS involves matrix operations (Cholesky solve, inversion) which are generally more expensive, scaling with the dimensionality of the covariance matrix [S4, unofficial].
 *   **Memory Complexity:** VIPER and Depth Measure require minimal additional memory (scalar values) [S2, S3, unofficial]. UBS requires storage for covariance matrices and their factors [S4, unofficial].
 *   **Strengths:** VIPER provides bright, clear surface rendering [S2, unofficial]. Depth Measure reveals occluded internal structures and preserves local contrast [S3, unofficial]. UBS provides statistically grounded opacity and parameter compensation [S4, unofficial].
